---
import { getEntry } from "astro:content";
import ProductLayout from "../../../layouts/ProductLayout.astro";

const app = (await getEntry("apps", "cookfrom"))!;
---
<ProductLayout
  app={app}
  tab="support"
  route="supportCookfrom"
  title="CookFrom Support — HomeLabCore"
  description="Help with CookFrom: troubleshooting AI recipe generation, ingredient photo recognition, Pro entitlement and purchase restoration, and application data. Contact support@homelabcore.dev."
  ogTitle="CookFrom Support"
  ogDescription="Help with CookFrom: AI recipe generation, ingredient photo recognition, Pro entitlement and purchase restoration, and application data."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>CookFrom Support</h1>
      <p class="lead">Below are answers to the most common questions. If none of them solve your problem, email us and include your device model, Android version, and a short description of what happened.</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="mailto:support@homelabcore.dev">Email CookFrom support</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/privacy/cookfrom">Privacy questions</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="ai-recipes">AI recipe generation</h2>
      <p>If recipe generation fails or seems stuck:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Check your internet connection — AI recipe generation needs to reach our backend.</li>
        <li>Try again after a short wait; a request can fail temporarily.</li>
        <li>Make sure you have selected at least a few ingredients before generating.</li>
        <li>If you have reached your current AI usage allowance, generation may be limited until it resets or until you have CookFrom Pro.</li>
        <li>Restart the app if it has been open in the background for a long time.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>AI-generated recipes can contain mistakes. Always check a recipe yourself before cooking, especially against your allergies.</p>

      <h2 id="photo-recognition">Ingredient photo recognition</h2>
      <p>If ingredients are not recognized correctly from a photo:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Grant the app camera or photo permission if prompted.</li>
        <li>Use good lighting and photograph items separately or clearly spaced out.</li>
        <li>Avoid heavy shadows, packaging glare, or very cluttered backgrounds.</li>
        <li>Recognition needs an internet connection; check your connection and try again.</li>
        <li>You can always add or correct ingredients manually after recognition.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="pro-entitlement">Pro entitlement and purchase restoration</h2>
      <p>If CookFrom Pro is not showing as active after a purchase, or after reinstalling or switching devices:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Make sure you are signed in to the same Google account that made the purchase.</li>
        <li>Open the app while online so it can re-verify your subscription with Google Play.</li>
        <li>Look for a "restore purchases" option in the app's Pro or settings screen and run it.</li>
        <li>Confirm the subscription is active in the Google Play <em>Subscriptions</em> screen.</li>
        <li>If it still does not appear, email us from the account used for the purchase and include the approximate purchase date.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Payments and refunds are handled by Google Play. Refund requests should be made through Google Play.</p>

      <h2 id="app-data">Application data</h2>
      <p>Your pantry, shopping list, favorites, recipe history, and preferences are stored on your device.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Clearing the app's data or uninstalling CookFrom removes information stored on the device and cannot be undone.</li>
        <li>If the app behaves incorrectly, first try restarting it, then restarting your device.</li>
        <li>If a screen fails to load repeatedly, make sure the app is updated to the latest version.</li>
        <li>To request deletion of data associated with your installation or subscription held by our backend, contact us at the privacy address below.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>For help with CookFrom, email <a href="mailto:support@homelabcore.dev">support@homelabcore.dev</a>.</p>
      <p>For questions about how CookFrom handles your data, see the <a href="/privacy/cookfrom">CookFrom Privacy Policy</a> or email <a href="mailto:privacy@homelabcore.dev">privacy@homelabcore.dev</a>.</p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p>When you email support, including your device model, Android version, app version, and the steps that led to the problem helps us understand the issue on the first reply.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ProductLayout>
